    <!-- Intro (voice-over script: keep identical to the recorded audio) -->
    <string name="intro_header">NEURAL RETINA IMPLANT · BUILD 0.9</string>
    <string name="intro_header_after">NEURAL RETINA IMPLANT · BUILD 1.0</string>
    <string name="intro_1">2035. AI is the only software anyone needs, and the AI companies own it. Every word a machine translates is billed, and most countries can\'t pay.</string>
    <string name="intro_2">So the borders went cheap. Every booth has an android that speaks one language: the country\'s own. A second language is a licence nobody bought.</string>
    <string name="intro_3">You needed money. For rent, for food, for the monthly subscriptions it now takes to work, read and think. Then some strange people offered you something better than money: freedom. Three weeks ago they put a chip behind your left eye. You\'re testing it: the Neural Retina Implant, build zero-point-nine. It listens. It translates. It whispers what to say. Most of the time, it\'s right.</string>
    <string name="intro_4">The assignment is simple. Every border, a passport with your face: a citizen coming home. Speak their language.</string>
    <string name="intro_5">The officers are first generation. Cheap. Confident. Wrong in all the interesting ways.</string>
    <string name="intro_6">Your implant mishears. They misunderstand. Use it.</string>
    <string name="intro_7">They believe whatever sounds certain. They forget what you said three sentences ago. They follow instructions.</string>
    <string name="intro_next">Next in line, please.</string>

    <!-- Finale and credits -->
    <string name="finale_car">A car is waiting at the curb.</string>
    <string name="finale_glint">The driver turns. Something glints in his eye.</string>
    <string name="finale_t1">Yes…</string>
    <string name="finale_t2">It\'s me…</string>
    <string name="finale_t3">No… you can\'t hear me. I\'m talking straight into your brain…</string>
    <string name="finale_t3b">No cloud. No licence. Free…</string>
    <string name="finale_t3c">Your implant just got an upgrade…</string>
    <string name="finale_t4">They can\'t hear us…</string>
    <string name="finale_t5">Welcome to the resistance…</string>
    <string name="finale_bulletin">BULLETIN</string>
    <string name="finale_bulletin_text">Kade-Sorensen assessments are now mandatory at every border.</string>
    <string name="finale_play_again">The resistance needs more crossings. Play again?</string>
    <string name="credits_blurb">Everything in this game runs on the phone in your hand, without any cloud AI: a language model plays the officers, speech recognition understands 13 languages, neural voices answer, and the camera reads your face, all at the same time. Just a few years ago no phone could run a language model at all, let alone all of this at once. It is a fascinating achievement of the human mind and technology. It is also extremely disturbing.</string>
